# PA-EP-003 — Enterprise Logical Information Model (ELIM)

**Project:** BTA V5.1 — HCGO Enterprise Persistence Architecture

**Status:** Approved

**Classification:** Persistence Architecture

---

# Purpose

Establish the authoritative Enterprise Logical Information Model (ELIM) for HCGO.

The Enterprise Logical Information Model (ELIM) organizes Enterprise Information Categories into logical enterprise structures while faithfully preserving the Enterprise Conceptual Information Model (ECIM).

The Enterprise Logical Information Model remains independent of physical persistence technologies.

It identifies logical organization only.

It does not define PostgreSQL, tables, schemas, columns, foreign keys, indexes, APIs, runtime execution, messaging, or technology implementation.

---

# Architecture Objective

Establish the authoritative logical organization of Enterprise Information Categories independently of persistence technology.

The Enterprise Logical Information Model organizes enterprise information for logical consistency while preserving the conceptual enterprise semantics established by:

- Constitutional Governance
- Enterprise Discovery
- Enterprise Analysis
- Enterprise Persistence Architecture
- Enterprise Conceptual Information Model

The Enterprise Logical Information Model serves as the authoritative logical bridge between conceptual enterprise semantics and physical persistence architecture.

---

# Enterprise Logical Information Model

The Enterprise Logical Information Model shall identify:

- Logical Enterprise Information Groups
- Enterprise Information Categories
- Enterprise Logical Relationships
- Enterprise Logical Dependencies
- Enterprise Logical Constraints
- Enterprise Logical Ownership
- Enterprise Logical Stewardship
- Enterprise Logical Boundaries

For every Enterprise Information Category identify:

- Logical Information Group
- Enterprise Information Category
- Logical Definition
- Authoritative Owner
- Logical Relationships
- Logical Dependencies
- Logical Constraints
- Logical Boundaries
- Ownership Notes

---

# Enterprise Logical Information Model Does NOT Identify

The Enterprise Logical Information Model shall not identify:

- PostgreSQL tables
- Schemas
- Columns
- Primary Keys
- Foreign Keys
- Indexes
- SQL
- Database normalization
- APIs
- Runtime execution
- Service implementation
- Physical persistence
- Technology implementation

Those responsibilities belong to subsequent Physical Persistence Architecture and Technology Implementation phases.

