# Enterprise Logical Organization

The Enterprise Logical Information Model organizes Enterprise Information Categories into logical enterprise structures while preserving conceptual authority.

Logical organization shall include, at a minimum:

- Enterprise Communication Normalization
- Enterprise Understanding
- Expert Identity
- Source Identity
- Participation Authorization
- Domain Definition
- Governance Metadata
- Enterprise Audit Evidence
- Platform Configuration
- Enterprise Capability Definition

Additional logical enterprise structures may be introduced through approved enterprise governance without redefining conceptual enterprise semantics.

