# Architectural Observation — Enterprise Semantics Precede Logical Modeling

Traditional persistence methodologies commonly follow this progression:

Conceptual Model

↓

Logical Model

↓

Physical Model

HCGO introduces an additional architectural foundation that precedes conceptual modeling.

The HCGO progression becomes:

Constitutional Governance

↓

Enterprise Discovery

↓

Enterprise Analysis

↓

Enterprise Persistence Architecture

↓

Enterprise Conceptual Information Model

↓

Enterprise Logical Information Model

↓

Physical Persistence Model

↓

Technology Implementation

---

# Architectural Rationale

By the time the Enterprise Logical Information Model is developed, the enterprise semantic model has already been established and validated through:

- Constitutional Governance
- Enterprise Discovery
- Enterprise Analysis
- Enterprise Persistence Architecture
- Enterprise Conceptual Information Model

Accordingly, the responsibility of the Enterprise Logical Information Model is not to define enterprise semantics.

Its responsibility is to faithfully organize previously established enterprise semantics into a logical enterprise structure suitable for subsequent physical persistence design.

The Enterprise Logical Information Model is therefore an organizational artifact rather than a semantic discovery artifact.

---

# Constitutional Principle

Enterprise semantics always precede conceptual representation.

Conceptual representation always precedes logical organization.

Logical organization always precedes physical representation.

Physical representation always precedes technology implementation.

Each architectural phase faithfully represents the authoritative outcomes established by the previous phase.

No architectural or implementation phase may redefine authoritative enterprise decisions established by an earlier phase except through approved Constitutional Governance.

---

# Architecture Outcome

The Enterprise Logical Information Model becomes the authoritative logical organization of enterprise information across HCGO.

It faithfully represents:

- Constitutional Governance
- Enterprise Discovery
- Enterprise Analysis
- Enterprise Persistence Architecture
- Enterprise Conceptual Information Model

All subsequent Physical Persistence Models shall faithfully implement the Enterprise Logical Information Model.

No Physical Persistence Model or Technology Implementation may redefine:

- Enterprise Concepts
- Enterprise Information Categories
- Enterprise Information Definitions
- Enterprise Authorities
- Enterprise Ownership
- Enterprise Stewardship
- Enterprise Relationships
- Enterprise Constraints
- Enterprise Information Boundaries
- Enterprise Ownership Boundaries
- Enterprise Stewardship Boundaries
- Enterprise Logical Organization

