# Current Assessment

The Enterprise Logical Information Model establishes the authoritative logical organization of enterprise information across HCGO.

It organizes previously validated enterprise semantics into a logical enterprise structure while preserving constitutional governance, enterprise authority, ownership, stewardship, traceability, lifecycle governance, and conceptual boundaries.

The Enterprise Logical Information Model remains the authoritative bridge between the Enterprise Conceptual Information Model and Physical Persistence Architecture.

No subsequent persistence or implementation artifact may redefine the enterprise semantics or logical organization established by the Enterprise Logical Information Model.

This preserves complete architectural traceability from Constitutional Governance through final technology implementation.